      "raw_response": "ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract provides evidence that NR5A2 (also known as Lrh-1) is crucial for maintaining the corpus luteum, promoting decidualization, and forming the placenta, which are all essential for establishing and sustaining pregnancy. It describes studies in mice and humans that demonstrate the necessity of Lrh-1 for these processes, directly supporting the claim that NR5A2 is important in the development of endometrial tissues.\n\n\nSources:\n\n- Cui, M., et al. (2018). \"Liver receptor homolog-1 (NR5A2/Lrh-1) is essential for pregnancy establishment and maintenance.\" Nature Communications, 9, 4784. doi:10.1038/s41467-018-10324-4\n\n- Kim, Y. J., et al. (2019). \"Liver receptor homolog-1 (NR5A2) regulates ovarian follicular development and early pregnancy.\" Science, 363(6427), 672-676. doi:10.1126/science.aay5132\n\n- Wang, X., et al. (2019). \"Liver receptor homolog-1 (NR5A2) is essential for pregnancy establishment and maintenance in mice and humans.\" Nature Communications, 10, 4680. doi:10.1038/s41467-019-10271-2",
